---
import { TAGS_IN_USE, TREE } from '@lib/features/project-knowledge-base';
---

<section class="border-t border-line" aria-labelledby="kb-structure-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-6">
      <h2 id="kb-structure-title" class="h2">
        A tree three levels deep, and nothing else to learn.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5 max-w-[50ch]">
        There are no separate categories. An article with articles under it is the category, and it can carry its own
        overview. Drag an article to reorder it or move it under another; from the keyboard, <code>Alt</code> with the
        arrow keys does the same. Moving it never changes its address.
      </p>
      <div class="rule-list mt-8">
        <div class="py-5">
          <h3 class="h3">Comments</h3>
          <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
            The same editing and deleting rules as comments on issues, and <code>@username</code> mentions work the same
            way.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="py-5">
          <h3 class="h3">Files</h3>
          <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
            Drop or paste them into the editor, or attach them to a comment. Up to 50 per article, counted toward the
            organisation's storage like any other attachment.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="py-5">
          <h3 class="h3">Addresses that last</h3>
          <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
            <em>Restoring a failed sync</em> becomes <code>restoring-a-failed-sync</code>. Renaming keeps the address,
            so links and agent references keep working.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="py-5">
          <h3 class="h3">Restore for 14 days</h3>
          <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
            A deleted article comes back from <strong>Deleted articles</strong>, with anything deleted along with it.
            There is no version history: each article shows who changed it last, and when.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:col-span-5 lg:col-start-8">
      <figure class="kb-rail panel" aria-labelledby="kb-rail-caption">
        <div class="pane-bar">
          <span class="mono text-xs">ACME</span>
          <span class="sep">/</span>
          <span class="text-fg">Knowledge base</span>
        </div>
        <div class="kb-rail-body">
          <p class="kb-rail-head">Starred</p>
          <p class="kb-node kb-l1">
            <span class="kb-star" aria-hidden="true">
              ★
            </span>
            Restoring a failed sync
          </p>

          <p class="kb-rail-head mt-4">Articles</p>
          <ul>
            {TREE.map((article, index) => (
              <li
                class:list={[
                  'kb-node',
                  `kb-l${article.level}`,
                  { 'kb-open': article.open, 'kb-is-draft': article.draft },
                ]}
              >
                <span class:list={['kb-chev', { 'kb-chev-open': !article.folded }]} aria-hidden="true">
                  {article.folded || (TREE[index + 1]?.level ?? 0) > article.level ? '›' : ''}
                </span>
                <span class="kb-node-title">{article.title}</span>
                {article.draft && <span class="kb-draft">Draft</span>}
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>

          <p class="kb-rail-head mt-4">Tags</p>
          <ul class="kb-cloud">
            {TAGS_IN_USE.map(item => (
              <li>
                {item.tag}
                <span>{item.count}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <figcaption id="kb-rail-caption" class="kb-rail-foot">
          The side panel beside every knowledge base page: starred articles, the tree, and the tags in use with how many
          articles carry each. Click a tag to filter by it.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .kb-rail {
    max-width: 380px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1023px) {
    .kb-rail {
      max-width: none;
    }
  }
  .kb-rail-body {
    padding: 14px 12px 16px;
    background: var(--bg-app);
  }
  .kb-rail-head {
    padding: 0 8px 4px;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .kb-node {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    height: 28px;
    padding-right: 8px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .kb-l1 {
    padding-left: 8px;
  }
  .kb-l2 {
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  .kb-l3 {
    padding-left: 36px;
  }
  .kb-node-title {
    min-width: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }
  .kb-chev {
    width: 8px;
    flex: none;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .kb-chev-open {
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }
  .kb-star {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .kb-open {
    background: var(--bg-active);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .kb-open::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 6px;
    bottom: 6px;
    width: 2px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  .kb-is-draft {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .kb-draft {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    height: 18px;
    padding: 0 5px;
    border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: none;
  }
  .kb-cloud {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
    padding: 2px 8px 0;
  }
  .kb-cloud li {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    height: 24px;
    padding: 0 8px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--border);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .kb-cloud span {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .kb-rail-foot {
    padding: 12px 16px 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 19px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
</style>
